  "baseline_note": "The accepted base already contains the attempt-4 source verbatim. Fresh baseline comparison reproduces 80.58929%. Attempts 1-3 were inspected with git show and the supplied diagnosis. Registration already uses canonical GC/1.3 with -use_lmw_stmw on and remains NonMatching.",
  "hypotheses": [
    "A cast to integer-address addition alone still strength-reduces to a walking pointer (79.55357%, 204 bytes).",
    "Aligning the running byte offset in place removes the eighth saved register, but slot base and byte offset allocation still diverge; best declaration order measures 80.89286%.",
    "Narrowing the loop variable adds an unwanted zero-extension at the loop comparison; narrow only the subscript instead. Since index visits only 0..11, unsigned-short conversion preserves every accessed element and all side effects. This removes the redundant offset recurrence and recovers retail r25-r31 allocation, lwzx and stwx.",
    "Register storage annotations and treating the table base as an integer do not improve the in-place-alignment form."
  ],
  "retained_variant": "narrow_subscript",
